 - **Symptom:** (Android, Qualcomm's driver, Adreno 840) once indirect mesh draws draw, foliage shows as glowing white zig-zag spikes that converge on the centre of the screen, and the frame around them is over-exposed.
 - **Cause:** open. The game draws its foliage twice: a depth-only prepass (colour write mask 0, depth write, LESS) and a colour pass of the same instances that tests EQUAL against it. The colour pass alone, with the prepass skipped and EQUAL relaxed to LEQUAL, draws the foliage right, so the instance records and every binding are right. The prepass mesh draws alone draw the spikes: some primitives reference vertex slots that were never written (an unwritten slot is clip (0, 0, 0, 1), the centre of the screen). Ruled out by experiment: barriers, uniform and storage buffers, the lane source (`SubgroupLocalInvocationId` vs `LocalInvocationIndex`), depth clamp, and the colour mask (the prepass with mask 0xf draws the same spikes). The prepass and colour pass use different mesh modules; the likely cause is Qualcomm's compiler on the prepass modules; not proven.
-- **Workaround (stopgap, not a fix):** the profile key `mesh_prepass_skip` lists the prepass mesh shaders. On Qualcomm's driver their draws are skipped when they are depth-only (depth write on, no colour channel written), and draws of the paired colour pass mesh shaders that test EQUAL test LEQUAL instead (`vka_draw.c` `mesh_cut`). On Turnip (no `VK_EXT_mesh_shader`) no mesh draw draws, so no foliage either way. Cost: the objects write no depth (the colour pass has depth write off), so later passes that read the scene depth (fog, shadows, ambient occlusion) may differ slightly where they are. `DM_VK_MESH_PREPASS_SKIP=0` turns it off, `=1` applies it on every driver.
+- **Workaround (stopgap, not a fix):** the profile key `mesh_prepass_skip` lists the prepass mesh shaders. On Qualcomm's driver their draws are skipped when they are depth-only (depth write on, no colour channel written), and draws of the paired colour pass mesh shaders that test EQUAL test LEQUAL instead (`vka_draw.c` `mesh_cut`). On Turnip (no `VK_EXT_mesh_shader`) no mesh draw draws, so no foliage either way. Candidate correction (not checked on a phone): paired depth-tested, read-only EQUAL colour draws now enable depth writes with LEQUAL, so depth consumers after the colour pass can see the surface. Other comparisons, depth-writing draws and disabled depth tests retain their original state. Consumers before that colour pass still see the skipped prepass; the driver fault remains open. The production state conversion is covered across 64 combinations in `test_vka_mesh_depth.py`. `DM_VK_MESH_PREPASS_SKIP=0` turns it off, `=1` applies it on every driver.
